  q(TIME,'Which is the usual priority order for collections?','STAT, timed, fasting, then routine',['Routine, fasting, timed, then STAT','Fasting, routine, STAT, then timed','Timed, routine, fasting, then STAT'],'B','Urgent needs come first, then tests that depend on specific times.',BM),
  q(TIME,'Why should fasting patients be drawn early on morning rounds?','So they can eat breakfast sooner',['So their results take longer','So they skip lunch as well','So they miss their medications'],'C','Drawing early prevents patients from going too long without food.',BM),
  q(TIME,'What should be recorded on a timed specimen label?','The actual time it was drawn',['The time it was ordered only','The time of the next meal','The phlebotomist’s break time'],'D','Accurate times are needed to read results for tests like cortisol or drug levels.',BM),
  q(TIME,'A specimen sat too long before reaching the lab and is no longer stable. What should happen?','It is recollected',['It is tested anyway','It is frozen and stored','It is relabeled as new'],'A','Unstable specimens can give false results that harm patient care.',BM),
  q(COMM,'Which is an example of nonverbal communication?','Eye contact and facial expression',['Explaining the procedure aloud','Reading the requisition form','Calling the patient by name'],'B','Body language can show confidence, caring or impatience to patients.',MC),
  q(COMM,'Why should a phlebotomist avoid medical jargon with patients?','Patients may not understand it',['Jargon is illegal to use','Patients prefer longer visits','It makes draws take longer'],'C','Plain language helps patients understand the procedure and feel more at ease.',MC),
  q(CLER,'Which information must appear on a lab requisition?','Ordering provider’s name',['Patient’s favorite color','Phlebotomist’s home address','Hospital cafeteria hours'],'D','The lab needs the ordering provider to report results and ask questions.',BM),
  q(CLER,'During computer downtime, how are lab orders usually handled?','Manual requisitions and labels',['All collections are cancelled','Orders are sent by text message','Patients write their own labels'],'A','Downtime procedures keep collections safe and organized until systems return.',BM),
  q(SAFE,'Which federal law requires the use of safer needle devices?','Needlestick Safety and Prevention Act',['Patient Self-Determination Act','Clinical Laboratory Improvement Act','Americans with Disabilities Act'],'B','The 2000 law updated OSHA’s Bloodborne Pathogens Standard to require safer sharps devices.',MC),
  q(SAFE,'Which fire extinguisher class is used for electrical fires?','Class C',['Class A','Class B','Class D'],'C','Class A is for ordinary combustibles and Class B is for flammable liquids.',MC),
  q(SAFE,'Which practice is not allowed in a laboratory work area?','Eating and drinking',['Wearing a lab coat','Washing your hands','Using a sharps box'],'D','Food and drink can become contaminated with infectious material.',MC),
  q(SAFE,'What color is the biohazard symbol on most sharps containers?','Red or orange-red',['Light sky blue','Bright lime green','Clear or white'],'A','The biohazard symbol warns that the contents may be infectious.',MC),
  q(SAFE,'How many doses are in the standard hepatitis B vaccine series for adults?','3 doses',['1 dose','5 doses','10 doses'],'B','Employers must offer the vaccine free to workers at risk of blood exposure.',MC),
  q(LEGAL,'Which organization offers a phlebotomy technician certification exam?','ASCP',['FDA','DEA','OSHA'],'C','Certifications from groups like ASCP and NHA show competence to employers.',MC),
  q(LEGAL,'A phlebotomist gossips about a patient’s HIV test with coworkers in the cafeteria. What is this?','A breach of confidentiality',['An approved shift report','A standard lab practice','A required public notice'],'D','Patient information should only be shared with those who need it for care.',MC),
  q(LEGAL,'A patient holds out an arm after the phlebotomist explains the draw. This is:','Implied consent',['Written consent','Informed refusal','Expressed refusal'],'A','Patients may still withdraw consent at any time during the procedure.',MC),
  q(LEGAL,'What should a phlebotomist do after drawing blood from the wrong patient?','Report it and complete an incident report',['Hide the error and relabel the tubes','Ask the patient to keep it quiet','Throw away the tubes and say nothing'],'B','Reporting errors protects patients and helps prevent future mistakes.',MC),
  q(TERM,'What is the antecubital fossa?','The front of the elbow',['The back of the knee joint','The palm of the hand','The side of the neck'],'C','The antecubital fossa contains the median cubital, cephalic and basilic veins.',BM),
  q(TERM,'What is the main function of leukocytes?','Fighting infection',['Carrying oxygen','Forming clots','Storing iron'],'D','Leukocytes are white blood cells, including neutrophils and lymphocytes.',BM),
  q(TERM,'Which vessels carry oxygen-rich blood away from the heart?','Arteries',['Veins','Venules','Lymph vessels'],'A','The pulmonary artery is an exception, carrying oxygen-poor blood to the lungs.',BM),
  q(TERM,'What does the suffix “-penia” mean?','A deficiency',['An excess','A tumor','A swelling'],'B','For example, thrombocytopenia means a low number of platelets.',BM)
